{"sections": [
  {"key": "arc", "title": "The arc", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue compounded at 46.6% a year from $6.91 billion in FY2017 to $215.9 billion in FY2026 [F1][F10][F211]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The path was not smooth: FY2023 revenue was flat at 0.2% growth and operating margin fell 21.6pp to 15.7% [D284][D299][F47]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "That trough came from $2.17 billion of inventory provisions against excess Ampere supply, particularly for expected demand in China [P35][P38]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The recovery was a step change: revenue rose 125.9% in FY2024 and 114.2% in FY2025, driven by data center compute and networking for accelerated computing and AI [D338][D393][P10][P16]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "FY2026 growth slowed to 65.5% as Data Center still contributed 60.2pp of the 65.5pp total [D448][D622]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "drivers", "title": "What drove growth", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Data Center grew from 19.9% of revenue in FY2018 to 89.7% in FY2026, contributing 60.2pp of FY2026's 65.5% growth [D598][D620][D622][D448]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Within it, Data Center computing grew 59% on Blackwell demand and networking grew 142% on NVLink for GB200 and GB300 systems [P8]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Networking contributed 14.1pp in FY2026 against 46.1pp from Compute, so the largest driver remains concentrated in one product line [D636][D629]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating income grew 60.1% against 65.5% revenue growth, an incremental margin of 57.3% [D449][D448][D475]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Diluted EPS grew 66.7% against 64.7% net income growth as the diluted share count fell 1.2% [D452][D450][D470]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "margins", "title": "Margins and costs", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating margin of 60.4% in FY2026 sits well above the 32.8% window median but below the 62.4% FY2025 high [F50][D813][D812]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Gross margin fell 3.9pp to 71.1% and drove the 2.0pp operating-margin decline, partly offset by R&D and SG&A leverage of 1.3pp and 0.6pp [D462][D463][D478][D479]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2026 Compute & Networking operating-income increase was partly offset by a $4.5 billion H20 excess-inventory and purchase-obligation charge [P7]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Operating expenses rose 41%, driven by compensation and benefits from employee growth and by compute and infrastructure costs [P9][P5]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Net margin held at 55.6% because other income of $11.1 billion, largely unrealized equity gains including Intel, offset a tax rate rising to 15.1% [F70][X120][P3][D434][P2]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "cash", "title": "Cash conversion", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating cash flow of $102.7 billion was 0.86x net income, below the 1.00x of FY2017, and free cash flow was 0.81x, the window low [F100][F60][D435][D8][D436][D826]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Free cash flow margin of 44.8% is near the 44.4% window median, with capex at 2.8% of revenue and 2.13x D&A [D432][D822][D431][D437]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Inventory grew 112.3% and receivables 66.8%, pushing days inventory to 125 and days sales outstanding to 65 [D474][D473][D446][D445]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Stock-based compensation of $6.4 billion was only 6.2% of operating cash flow, so conversion is diluted by working capital rather than non-cash add-backs [X80][D438]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "balance_sheet", "title": "Balance sheet and capital allocation", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Net cash fell to $2.1 billion, just 1.0% of revenue, from $34.7 billion a year earlier, as cash and investments dropped 75.5% to $10.6 billion [D441][D442][D386][D471][D439]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Investing outflow of $52.2 billion rose on higher equity investment purchases and a non-exclusive license agreement with Groq [F120][P1]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Net cash still ranks in the 83rd percentile of six semis peers against a median of -13.9% of revenue, and the current ratio is 3.91x [D844][D845][F190]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Buybacks and dividends of $41.1 billion absorbed 42.5% of free cash flow, and long-term debt fell 11.7% to $7.5 billion [D443][D444][F200][D459]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "red_flags", "title": "Red flags", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Customer concentration is the main risk: two direct customers were 22% and 14% of FY2026 revenue, both mainly in Compute & Networking [P6]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "China revenue fell 21.4% in FY2026, subtracting 4.1pp from growth, after contributing 20.9pp in FY2025 [D545][D546][D543]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The Graphics segment's 25% FY2023 decline was a one-period cyclical event, with segment revenue up 57.0% in FY2026, so it is not a persistent flag [D754][D747]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Product revenue members sum to 190% of consolidated revenue in FY2026 because some are totals of others, so segment shares must not be added [R2]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "watch", "title": "What to watch", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Gross margin: a further move below the 71.1% of FY2026 would confirm cost pressure from the H20 charge and product mix, reported in the FY2027 10-K [F30][P7]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Data Center share: holding above the 89.7% of FY2026 confirms the concentration trend, while a fall toward the 78.0% of FY2024 would signal broadening [D620][D614]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Free cash flow conversion: a ratio below the 0.81x window low of FY2026 would show working capital outgrowing earnings [D436][D826]."}
  ]}
]}
